@startuml ITI-Scheduling-WofConnect

' ============================================================
' IHE ITI Scheduling – WofConnect Profile Mapping
' Based on: https://profiles.ihe.net/ITI/Scheduling/1.0.0/
' ============================================================

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam ParticipantPadding 16
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderThickness 1

title **IHE ITI Scheduling 1.0.0 – WofConnect Profile Mapping**

actor "End User\n(Patient / Provider)" as User
box "Scheduling Client" #E8F4FD
  participant "Clinical System" as Client
end box

box "Scheduling Server  (WofConnect)" #FFF3E0
  participant "WOF Connect\nFHIR Server" as Server
end box

== **0 – Prerequisite: Discover Capabilities & Context** ==

note over Client, Server #FFFDE7
  **WofConnect-specific (beyond ITI Scheduling)**
  These operations provide scheduling context and
  capability discovery before the standard ITI flow.
end note

User -> Client : Open scheduling view
Client -> Server : **$wof-capabilities**  (system-level)
note right #E0F7FA
  **Response:**
  «WofConnectCapabilitiesCarrier»  (Basic)
  + ext: «WofConnectCharacteristic»
  (scheduling / workflow / security flags)
end note
Server --> Client : Basic resource

Client -> Server : **$get-schedule-context**  (Schedule type-level)
note right #E0F7FA
  **Input:** period-start, period-end,\nhealthcare-service, actor
  **Response Bundle:**
  «WofConnectScheduleContextOperationResponse»
  containing:
  ├ «WofConnectBillingOrganization»  (Organization)
  ├ «WofConnectHealthcareService»  (HealthcareService)
  ├ «WofConnectActivityDefinition»  (ActivityDefinition)
  ├ «WofConnectSchedule»  (Schedule)
  ├ «WofConnectPractitioner»  (Practitioner)
  └ «WofConnectPractitionerRole»  (PractitionerRole)
end note
Server --> Client : Bundle (searchset)

Client -> Server : GET Patient?identifier=<personnummer>
note right #E0F7FA
  **Response:** «WofConnectPatient»
  (identifier: personalNumber, name, birthDate, telecom)
end note
Server --> Client : Patient resource

== **1 – ITI-115: Find Potential Appointments  [$find]** //Required// ==

User -> Client : Select criteria\n(date range, provider, visit type)
Client -> Server : POST Appointment/**$find**
note right #C8E6C9
  **Input params:**
  • start (dateTime)
  • end (dateTime)
  • practitioner (Reference) – optional
  • organization (Reference) – optional
  • visit-type (string) – optional
end note
Server --> Client : **Bundle**
note right #C8E6C9
  «WofConnectFindAppointment»
  profiles: **ihe-sched-avail-bundle**
  entry[]:
  └ «WofConnectAppointment»
    profiles: **ihe-sched-appt**
    status = **proposed**
    + serviceType, start, end
    + identifier (SlotId)
    + participant[2] (actor + status)
end note

== **2 – ITI-116: Hold Appointment  [$hold]** //Optional// ==
note over Client, Server #FFF9C4
  WofConnect CapabilityStatement declares $hold as SHALL,
  but **no dedicated WofConnect profile** exists for this transaction.
  The standard **ihe-sched-appt** profile is used.
end note

User -> Client : Select appointment
Client -> Server : POST Appointment/**$hold**
Server --> Client : Bundle (held Appointment)

== **3 – ITI-117: Book Appointment  [$book]** //Required// ==

User -> Client : Confirm booking /\nModify / Cancel

group **CREATE** [status = pending, no existing id]
  Client -> Server : POST Appointment/**$book**
  note right #C8E6C9
    **Input:**
    appointment resource
    (status = **pending**)
  end note
end

group **MODIFY** [status = booked, existing id, updated details]
  Client -> Server : POST Appointment/**$book**
  note right #C8E6C9
    **Input:**
    appointment resource
    (status = **booked**, existing id)
  end note
end

group **CANCEL** [status = cancelled, existing id]
  Client -> Server : POST Appointment/**$book**
  note right #C8E6C9
    **Input:**
    appointment resource
    (status = **cancelled**, existing id)
  end note
end

Server --> Client : **Bundle**
note right #C8E6C9
  «WofConnectFindAppointment» (Bundle)
  entry[]:
  └ «WofConnectBookingAppointment»
    profiles: **ihe-sched-appt**
    status = **booked** | **cancelled** | **fulfilled**
    + ext: «WofBaseCharacteristic»
    + ext: «WofBaseAppointmentUpdate»
      (canBeRescheduled, canBeCancelled,
       webReschedulingCount)
    + serviceType, start, end
    + participant[2], reasonCode
end note

== **4 – ITI-118: Find Existing Appointments  [FHIR Search]** //Optional// ==

Client -> Server : GET Appointment?patient=<id>&date=<range>
Server --> Client : **Bundle** (searchset)
note right #C8E6C9
  Contains existing
  «WofConnectBookingAppointment» resources
end note

== **Supporting Resource Access (read / search)** ==

note over Client, Server #F3E5F5
  Standard FHIR REST interactions on supporting resources.
  All profiled by WofConnect.
end note

Client -> Server : GET HealthcareService?identifier=<id>
note right #F3E5F5: «WofConnectHealthcareService»
Client -> Server : GET Organization?identifier=<id>
note right #F3E5F5: «WofConnectBillingOrganization»
Client -> Server : GET PractitionerRole?service=<ref>
note right #F3E5F5: «WofConnectPractitionerRole»
Client -> Server : GET Practitioner/<id>
note right #F3E5F5: «WofConnectPractitioner»
Client -> Server : GET ActivityDefinition?code=<code>
note right #F3E5F5: «WofConnectActivityDefinition»
Client -> Server : GET Schedule?actor=<ref>&service-type=<token>
note right #F3E5F5: «WofConnectSchedule»

@enduml
